From fd24806d7f70521068674ade0b2f245b652bc8bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Anderson <chris@raitechnology.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 20:03:03 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] overlayfs: accept non-casefolded dentries on a
 casefold-capable fs

Android formats userdata with the f2fs casefold feature; with CONFIG_UNICODE
the filesystem then installs generic_ci_d_hash/d_compare on every dentry and
ovl_dentry_weird() refused any upper or lower dir under /data ("filesystem on
'...' not supported"), so an OCI runtime in an AOHP env (podman, crun) fell
back to fuse-overlayfs. The ci ops are exact-match unless the directory itself
carries the casefold flag, so only refuse dentries that are really casefolded.
Same direction as mainline 6.13 "ovl: Support case-insensitive filesystems",
limited to what 5.10 overlayfs needs.

Seen on the Solana Saga (sm8475, encoding UTF-8 12.1.0); the OnePlus 13's
userdata has no casefold encoding and never hit it. 2026-11-09.

Change-Id: Icca6ff066b6581bf00e36a5f0148f0bde4d13727
---
 fs/overlayfs/util.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fs/overlayfs/util.c b/fs/overlayfs/util.c
index ed525ea31ccf..14fec831de1e 100644
--- a/fs/overlayfs/util.c
+++ b/fs/overlayfs/util.c
@@ -144,13 +144,29 @@ void ovl_dentry_init_flags(struct dentry *dentry, struct dentry *upperdentry,
 
 bool ovl_dentry_weird(struct dentry *dentry)
 {
+	unsigned int flags;
+
 	if (!d_can_lookup(dentry) && !d_is_file(dentry) && !d_is_symlink(dentry))
 		return true;
 
-	return dentry->d_flags & (DCACHE_NEED_AUTOMOUNT |
-				  DCACHE_MANAGE_TRANSIT |
-				  DCACHE_OP_HASH |
-				  DCACHE_OP_COMPARE);
+	flags = dentry->d_flags & (DCACHE_NEED_AUTOMOUNT |
+				   DCACHE_MANAGE_TRANSIT |
+				   DCACHE_OP_HASH |
+				   DCACHE_OP_COMPARE);
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_UNICODE)
+	/*
+	 * AOHP: a casefold-capable filesystem (Android userdata is formatted
+	 * with the f2fs casefold feature) installs the case-insensitive
+	 * hash/compare ops on every dentry, but generic_ci_d_hash/compare
+	 * fall back to the exact-match behaviour unless the directory itself
+	 * has the casefold flag. Only refuse dentries that are really
+	 * casefolded, so an OCI runtime's overlay storage under /data works.
+	 */
+	if (dentry->d_sb->s_encoding && d_inode(dentry) &&
+	    !IS_CASEFOLDED(d_inode(dentry)))
+		flags &= ~(DCACHE_OP_HASH | DCACHE_OP_COMPARE);
+#endif
+	return flags;
 }
 
 enum ovl_path_type ovl_path_type(struct dentry *dentry)
-- 
